  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 1200 AM CDT Tue Sep 22 2026\n\nThursday through Monday:\n\nHigh pressure continues to influence the pattern in the second \nhalf of the week as it gradually shifts east. Expect lighter \nwinds through the end of the week resulting in improving swim \nrisk conditions Thursday for all southern WI beaches. Otherwise,\ncontinue to see the trend in the medium range models of an \nupper-level ridge building across the Upper Midwest into the \nweekend. This will not only bring a drier pattern, but also \nshould begin to see temps gradually warm each day into the \nweekend. There is even a potential (20-40% per LREF members) to\nsee high temps rise back into the 70s toward the end of the \nweekend into the start of next week. \n\nWagner",
